@startuml sequence_shutdown
title Service Shutdown Sequence (Nomad signals → ServiceRunner drain → Consul deregister)

participant "Operator" as op
participant "Manager GUI" as gui
participant "FastAPI bridge\n(/api/nomad/*)" as bridge
participant "Nomad server" as ns
participant "Nomad client" as nc
participant "wrapper.bat / .py" as wrapper
participant "ServiceRunner\n(in service process)" as runner
participant "grpc::Server" as grpc
participant "Consul agent" as consul

== Phase 1: User initiates stop ==

op -> gui : Click "Stop job"\nin Service Network tab
gui -> bridge : POST /api/nomad/jobs/<id>/stop
activate bridge
bridge -> ns : DELETE /v1/job/<id>
activate ns
ns --> bridge : 200 OK\nstop_evaluation_id
deactivate bridge

== Phase 2: Nomad propagates the stop ==

ns -> nc : task stop directive\nfor allocation <alloc-id>
deactivate ns
activate nc

nc -> wrapper : send SIGTERM (Linux)\nor CTRL_BREAK_EVENT (Windows)
activate wrapper

== Phase 3: Signal reaches ServiceRunner ==

wrapper -> runner : signal forwarded to child
note right of runner
  signal.signal(SIGBREAK,\n  signal.default_int_handler)\nensures Windows SIGBREAK becomes\nKeyboardInterrupt → finally blocks\nrun (otherwise default handler\ncalls ExitProcess and skips cleanup).
end note

activate runner

runner -> runner : signal handler sets\nshutdown flag
runner -> grpc : Server::Shutdown(deadline=5s)
activate grpc

note right of grpc
  In-flight RPCs given the deadline
  to complete.  New RPCs receive
  UNAVAILABLE.
end note

grpc -> grpc : drain in-flight streams
grpc --> runner : drained
deactivate grpc

== Phase 4: Consul deregistration ==

runner -> consul : PUT /v1/agent/service/deregister/<id>
activate consul
consul -> consul : remove instance from catalog
consul --> runner : 200 OK
deactivate consul

note over consul
  Any client that does
  GET /v1/health/service/<name>?passing
  immediately after no longer sees
  this instance — no stale endpoints.
end note

== Phase 5: Process exit ==

runner --> wrapper : main() returns\nor sys.exit(0)
deactivate runner
wrapper --> nc : exit code 0
deactivate wrapper
nc -> ns : alloc status: complete
deactivate nc

== Phase 6: GUI confirms ==

gui -> bridge : GET /api/consul/health/<name>\n(periodic refresh)
activate bridge
bridge -> consul : GET /v1/health/service/<name>?passing
activate consul
consul --> bridge : [] (empty — instance is gone)
deactivate consul
bridge --> gui : empty list
deactivate bridge

note over gui
  Sidebar drops the service entry;
  if the service detail panel was
  open for it, the right pane clears
  (see ServiceCreator.js: active panel
   is deactivated when the service name
   is no longer in MM.servicesInfor).
end note

== Hard-kill fallback (only if Phase 3 timeouts) ==

note over nc, wrapper
  If ServiceRunner doesn't exit within
  the kill_timeout (default 5s), Nomad
  follows up with SIGKILL / TerminateProcess.
  Consul TTL eventually reaps the entry
  (~30s default) — but with kill_signal +
  graceful runner code, this path is rare.
end note

@enduml
